      "card_ids": ["C15", "C43", "C12", "C19", "C20", "C04", "C13"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic metabolism records are mechanistically consistent with presystemic loss: a secondary-amine phenethylamine analog is metabolized by multiple CYPs (C93); an indole-containing analog has HLM intrinsic clearances of 8.7 and 16.5 µL/min/mg for hydroxylation/glucuronidation (C90, C91); a cinnamohydroxamate analog has HLM t1/2 of 33 min (C86, C88); and a tryptoline analog has human/mouse CLint of 12/21 µL/min/mg (C92).",
      "card_ids": ["C93", "C90", "C91", "C86", "C88", "C92"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The tertiary-amine hydroxamate analog with high Papp and no significant efflux (C77) does not transfer because the query is a secondary amine, matching the low-permeability/high-efflux M02 rather than M03.",
      "card_ids": ["C77", "C73"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Low-clearance L6 records for rebamipide (C82, C85) and carnosic acid (C83, C84, C87, C89) are not transferable to the query because those molecules lack the query's secondary amine and hydroxamic acid; they do not undermine the low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C82", "C85", "C83", "C84", "C87", "C89"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "High-F contexts such as tadalafil (36-80%) and ketanserin (~50%) are structurally dissimilar, and fluvastatin is borderline (24-29% in L1, 10-35% in L2); they do not outweigh the low-F tryptamine and poor-permeability analogs.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C11", "C21", "C26", "C02", "C10", "C25", "C28", "C03", "C06", "C07", "C14", "C37", "C40"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C86", "C88", "C90", "C91", "C92", "C93"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2/PAMPA, intestinal metabolism, or in vivo PK is available; the closest L5 analog is a benzimidazole hydroxamate, not the query's indole.",
    "L6 hepatic clearance records are for analogs with different cores (benzimidazole, pyridine, tryptoline, diterpene) and do not provide a query-specific hepatic extraction ratio.",
    "HLM t1/2 for the closest cinnamohydroxamate analog is moderate (33 min), so the magnitude of hepatic first-pass loss remains uncertain.",
    "Low neutral fraction is a physicochemical prior, not endpoint proof; high-F contexts are structurally dissimilar."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low (F < 20%) because the query's tryptamine core, secondary amine, and zwitterionic low-neutral-fraction character align with transferable low-F contexts (DMT 10-15%, sumatriptan 14-15%, eluxadoline ~1%) and with L5 Caco-2 evidence that a secondary-amine hydroxamate analog has low Papp and high efflux. L6 hepatic metabolism records are mechanistically consistent with additional presystemic loss (CYP metabolism of a secondary-amine analog, substantial HLM intrinsic clearance for an indole-containing analog, moderate HLM t1/2 for a cinnamohydroxamate), but are not direct F measurements. High-F contexts are structurally dissimilar or borderline, so the low prediction is retained and modestly strengthened."
}

